---@class aws.lightsail.UpdateRelationalDatabaseRequest
---@field relationalDatabaseName aws.lightsail.ResourceName The name of your Lightsail database resource to update.
---@field masterUserPassword? aws.lightsail.SensitiveString|distilled.Secret The password for the master user. The password can include any printable ASCII character except "/", """, or "@".
---@field rotateMasterUserPassword? aws.lightsail.boolean When true, the master user password is changed to a new strong password generated by Lightsail.
---@field preferredBackupWindow? aws.lightsail.string The daily time range during which automated backups are created for your database if automated backups are enabled.
---@field preferredMaintenanceWindow? aws.lightsail.string The weekly time range during which system maintenance can occur on your database.
---@field enableBackupRetention? aws.lightsail.boolean When true, enables automated backup retention for your database.
---@field disableBackupRetention? aws.lightsail.boolean When true, disables automated backup retention for your database.
---@field publiclyAccessible? aws.lightsail.boolean Specifies the accessibility options for your database. A value of true specifies a database that is available to resources outside of your Lightsail account. A value of false specifies a database that is available only to your Lightsail resources in the same region as your database.
---@field applyImmediately? aws.lightsail.boolean When true, applies changes immediately. When false, applies changes during the preferred maintenance window. Some changes may cause an outage.
---@field caCertificateIdentifier? aws.lightsail.string Indicates the certificate that needs to be associated with the database.
---@field relationalDatabaseBlueprintId? aws.lightsail.string This parameter is used to update the major version of the database. Enter the blueprintId for the major version that you want to update to.

---@class aws.lightsail.UpdateRelationalDatabaseResult
---@field operations? aws.lightsail.OperationList An array of objects that describe the result of the action, such as the status of the request, the timestamp of the request, and the resources affected by the request.

